      "id": "s3",
      "concept": "First law of thermodynamics",
      "narration": "The first law says energy can't be created or destroyed, only transferred. In a closed system, the change in internal energy equals heat added minus work done by the system. For example, if you compress a gas, its internal energy increases because work is done on it.",
