      "id": "s5",
      "concept": "Clausius inequality",
      "narration": "The Clausius inequality shows that for any cyclic process, the integral of dQ over T is less than or equal to zero. This means heat transfer at a temperature is always less than or equal to the heat transfer at a higher temperature. It defines the direction of natural heat flow and links to entropy change.",
